1
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:24,957
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:27,687
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:37,517
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,917
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,597
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:46,677
So bright, so bold, but so elusive.

9
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:48,717
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:51,857
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,697
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,557
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:05,617
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:08,897
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:11,000
We live in wonder.

17
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,177
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:27,577
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:29,797
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:32,057
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:33,557
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:36,637
We don't want to live ordinary life.

24
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:39,717
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:42,560
We live in one another.

26
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:52,150
Orchaka!

27
00:01:52,233 --> 00:01:53,900
Terrible news! It's the king!

28
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:54,937
What do you mean?

29
00:01:55,020 --> 00:01:56,597
What's happened to his majesty?

30
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:57,980
He's disappeared!

31
00:01:58,720 --> 00:01:59,720
That's absurd!

32
00:02:00,140 --> 00:02:02,360
Have you searched everywhere? Yes!

33
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:05,994
We searched the palace, the
garden, and the storehouses!

34
00:02:06,420 --> 00:02:08,597
Could he have slipped away
in the middle of the night?

35
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:09,510
Impossible!

36
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:11,477
The king's security was airtight!

37
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:14,148
There's no way he could
have gotten past us!

38
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:15,630
But why?

39
00:02:15,713 --> 00:02:19,060
Why would the king hide
himself just before the battle?

40
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:20,790
Search!

41
00:02:20,873 --> 00:02:22,657
Check outside the palace and in the town!

42
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:23,570
Sir!

43
00:02:27,820 --> 00:02:31,720
If only Pell were here instead of
on reconnaissance and rain base,

44
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:34,060
he excels at tracking people.

45
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:37,917
What could have happened to his majesty?

46
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,280
I can't afford to act recklessly.

47
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:42,800
Damn it!

48
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:47,060
Lord Chaka, we have news
of the King! What is it?

49
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:48,960
Have you found him? Yes, sir.

50
00:02:49,220 --> 00:02:50,220
He's in Nanohana.

51
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:51,917
The information is certain.

52
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,317
Good. That's a relief.

53
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,537
Yes, but...

54
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:57,520
Well, sir, you see, it's not that simple.

55
00:02:58,320 --> 00:02:59,380
What is it?

56
00:03:06,380 --> 00:03:08,200
Why now, all of a sudden?

57
00:03:10,660 --> 00:03:12,860
Has he fallen as far as he can?

58
00:03:13,220 --> 00:03:15,500
Don't be so suspicious, Koza.

59
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:17,996
Why would he do something this crazy?

60
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:21,150
Koza.

61
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:25,580
You know his majesty's
character too well for that.

62
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:27,191
He would never betray us.

63
00:03:27,820 --> 00:03:29,879
That's what all you old people say.

64
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:34,317
I didn't come all the
way to you, but with you.

65
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:35,812
Just to please the king.

66
00:03:40,140 --> 00:03:42,937
The rebels were over a
hundred thousand strong now.

67
00:03:43,020 --> 00:03:44,120
Yes, I've heard.

68
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:46,598
And there have been casualties, too.

69
00:03:53,660 --> 00:03:54,780
It's nothing.

70
00:03:56,760 --> 00:04:01,760
A little rain and these suspicions
will vanish like fog. Yes.

71
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:04,930
What?

72
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:06,780
The canal's been destroyed.

73
00:04:07,260 --> 00:04:08,700
Who would do this?

74
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:12,080
Now, we can't bring water to the town.

75
00:04:14,620 --> 00:04:16,900
It hasn't rained for over a year.

76
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,620
Aramalu is done for.

77
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:25,660
Don't be so suspicious, Koza.

78
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:34,049
I don't want to suspect you,
but people are dying of thirst.

79
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:37,180
Maybe you're not using
it, but you do have it.

80
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:38,550
No.

81
00:04:38,633 --> 00:04:40,520
We must wait for natural rain.

82
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:43,660
To use dance powder is
to summon misfortune.

83
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:46,037
Just a small amount should be all right.

84
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:49,177
The rebellion might stop even
if there's just a little rain.

85
00:04:49,260 --> 00:04:52,380
It would only result in
an even greater calamity.

86
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:57,240
I understand your desperation, but
it's not as easy as you think, Koza.

87
00:04:57,540 --> 00:05:00,128
I can't stand to watch
towns dry up anymore!

88
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:02,080
I've got to do something!

89
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:10,336
You haven't changed a bit
from the old days, have you?

90
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:13,180
Yes, I have.

91
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:15,380
Now I can fight.

92
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:20,040
And I swear, I'll come back here.

93
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:25,600
And when I do, I'm going to
take your reign from you.

94
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:36,437
Jai, you mean...

95
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:38,060
What was that?

96
00:05:38,260 --> 00:05:39,620
You heard me right.

97
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:42,200
I've come here to apologize to you all.

98
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:48,380
It was none other than I, the ruler of
Alabasta, who stole all this country's reign.

99
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:54,460
My lord, surely you must be
joking with us. You must be.

100
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:55,680
I'm not joking.

101
00:05:56,220 --> 00:05:57,200
You're mad.

102
00:05:57,460 --> 00:06:00,977
You knew how desperate things were
and yet you only helped yourself.

103
00:06:01,060 --> 00:06:05,472
No decent ruler would be so selfish if
he knew his own people were in need.

104
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:10,380
How dare you, a common peasant, speak
disrespectfully to your lord and master.

105
00:06:11,540 --> 00:06:14,364
Even though I needn't
justify my actions to you,

106
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:17,517
I came to Nanohana to
apologize for what I've done.

107
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:18,940
What more do you want?

108
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:22,300
My brother died in Yuba thanks to you.

109
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:28,177
I didn't come all the way to
this town just to apologize.

110
00:06:28,260 --> 00:06:29,672
There is another reason.

111
00:06:30,260 --> 00:06:34,337
As you may know, Dance Powder is
outlawed by the world government.

112
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:37,380
If word got out that
it had been used here,

113
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:41,097
the marines would certainly take
action and destroy this country.

114
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:42,880
I cannot allow that.

115
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:46,297
You may also remember that
large amounts of dance powder

116
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:49,733
were found being smuggled out
of this town two years ago.

117
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,353
It is necessary to eliminate
all traces of that incident.

118
00:06:53,980 --> 00:06:55,860
Do I make myself clear?

119
00:06:57,100 --> 00:06:58,197
You mean...

120
00:06:58,280 --> 00:06:59,260
I do.

121
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:02,537
There is only one way to erase
this incident from our past.

122
00:07:02,620 --> 00:07:05,860
We must obliterate Nanohana
and everyone in it!

123
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:10,229
We have to die because
you're going to win?

124
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:11,760
That's insane!

125
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:13,440
Hey, King!

126
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:18,037
So it was all your fault after all! You...

127
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:20,473
you stole the rain and killed the towns!

128
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:24,420
I'll get even with you
for what you've done!

129
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:38,340
I'll make you pay for this.

130
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:39,931
Apple, are you all right?

131
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:41,540
Please, no.

132
00:07:45,820 --> 00:07:49,020
Men, burn it to the ground
and leave no one alive.

133
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:55,360
Koza, it's Koza.

134
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,600
Koza, it's been a while.

135
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:04,897
What are you doing?

136
00:08:04,980 --> 00:08:10,577
What I'm apologizing.

137
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:13,997
I thought I had made that
clear. Shut up! Just shut up!

138
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:17,177
Do you have any idea what you're doing
to the people who believed in you?

139
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:18,477
It is an insult.

140
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:22,117
Nevertheless, I am the one
who's been using dance powder.

141
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:23,557
I told you to shut up.

142
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:26,140
Why are you so angry? Kohza?

143
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:28,417
Surely even you behind us.

144
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:31,857
What I'm trying to do...

145
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:33,587
You cold, heartless bastard!

146
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:35,090
Don't...

147
00:08:35,173 --> 00:08:36,003
Don't you understand?

148
00:08:36,160 --> 00:08:38,677
Don't you know how these people
felt as they died of thirst?

149
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:41,320
They felt no hatred or anger towards you!

150
00:08:41,540 --> 00:08:44,837
It isn't the king's fault this is
happening to us, he's a great leader!

151
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:48,417
Those were the words on their lips as
they died, they never lost faith in you!

152
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:52,317
But now, you come here and apologize,
and what happens to their faith?

153
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:55,753
At least have the decency to
lie and say you're innocent!

154
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:08,040
Who's the leader?

155
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:15,180
Okay, kids, let's go!

156
00:09:16,020 --> 00:09:17,580
Didn't we fight?

157
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:21,480
Because the kingdom, because everyone,

158
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:25,660
wanted to know if you were innocent.

159
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:36,000
At the very least

160
00:09:39,060 --> 00:09:40,860
That's why I fought

161
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:49,720
I don't believe it

162
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:03,790
Showtime!

163
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:05,760
A giant ship's about to crash!

164
00:10:11,920 --> 00:10:13,780
What kind of ship is that?

165
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:34,640
It's only over!

166
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:44,860
For the big finale, that was sure easy.

167
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:48,440
Have we ever done
anything that wasn't easy?

168
00:10:52,940 --> 00:10:54,617
We pulled it off!

169
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:57,465
Now, let's light the
fires and get out of here!

170
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:01,600
It feels so good to get back into gear!

171
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:07,360
Koza, say something, Koza! Come on!

172
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:11,117
Look, the royal army has disappeared!

173
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:12,030
What?

174
00:11:13,860 --> 00:11:17,566
Was I the kingliest king you ever
saw back there, or was I not?

175
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:20,420
Yes, you were the
greatest, Mr. Barclay, sir!

176
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:24,177
Stop those fires!

177
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:26,757
The Royal Army started
the fires, then ran off!

178
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:27,670
Hurry!

179
00:11:27,753 --> 00:11:29,189
We've got to put them out!

180
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:32,420
Now all we have to do is meet up with Mr.

181
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:33,800
Two outside town.

182
00:11:34,700 --> 00:11:36,560
Alabarna's the grand climax.

183
00:11:38,180 --> 00:11:39,010
Hmm.

184
00:11:39,093 --> 00:11:40,419
Frankly, I'm looking forward to it.

185
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:44,437
You know my favorite word is vague.

186
00:11:44,520 --> 00:11:45,840
I love that word.

187
00:11:46,140 --> 00:11:49,297
The king's prospects of staying
king are exceedingly vague.

188
00:11:49,380 --> 00:11:50,968
The operation is a success.

189
00:11:51,060 --> 00:11:52,001
Where's Moochie?

190
00:11:52,100 --> 00:11:53,197
He's west of town, Mr.

191
00:11:53,280 --> 00:11:54,280
Toubon Clay, sir.

192
00:11:55,640 --> 00:12:00,097
What the the king turned into
some kind of weird ballerina.

193
00:12:00,180 --> 00:12:03,220
It's no use we can't stop him!

194
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:06,980
He wasn't the king.

195
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:11,600
This is bad everyone's been
tricked i have to tell them.

196
00:12:13,740 --> 00:12:18,157
What a naughty boy how
much do you think he knows?

197
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:22,680
That imbecile he had to
get careless and screw up.

198
00:12:23,300 --> 00:12:24,140
Who are you?

199
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:27,960
I don't suppose you'd stay
quiet if we asked you.

200
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:29,910
Water!

201
00:12:29,993 --> 00:12:30,823
We need more water!

202
00:12:30,906 --> 00:12:31,736
Wait!

203
00:12:31,819 --> 00:12:32,649
That's my water!

204
00:12:32,732 --> 00:12:33,562
Can't you pay for it?

205
00:12:33,645 --> 00:12:34,475
Not now, you idiot!

206
00:12:34,558 --> 00:12:35,720
The town's on fire!

207
00:12:35,860 --> 00:12:36,860
Put out the fire!

208
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:39,230
Useless.

209
00:12:39,313 --> 00:12:40,825
It's just burning too quickly.

210
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:43,177
We should escape while we still can.

211
00:12:43,260 --> 00:12:44,672
Don't give up yet, Koza.

212
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,257
You're not the type to just
give in and die like this.

213
00:12:47,340 --> 00:12:48,281
You gotta fight!

214
00:12:55,540 --> 00:12:56,370
What?

215
00:12:56,453 --> 00:12:57,540
Here, take Koza.

216
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:59,857
Hey, kid, say something. Damn.

217
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:01,469
Even children aren't safe.

218
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:04,630
What?

219
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:06,960
Don't try and talk, kid. I've gotcha.

220
00:13:07,380 --> 00:13:08,792
It's not what you think.

221
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,412
Everyone's been tricked.

222
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:13,110
Hang in there, son.

223
00:13:13,193 --> 00:13:14,023
Koza.

224
00:13:16,060 --> 00:13:19,360
This country must die.

225
00:13:20,740 --> 00:13:22,317
Contact all of our units.

226
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:25,377
This will be our final battle!

227
00:13:25,460 --> 00:13:30,437
Well, all right, but we still
don't have enough weapons.

228
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:33,057
No, we have plenty.

229
00:13:33,140 --> 00:13:36,037
Now you know that ship that
just crashed into town?

230
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:38,657
As fate would have it,
it's an armory ship.

231
00:13:38,740 --> 00:13:39,977
Wait, are you sure?

232
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:42,037
Yeah, it's full of weapons.

233
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:43,680
It's almost like...

234
00:13:44,780 --> 00:13:45,780
divine guidance.

235
00:13:49,100 --> 00:13:49,930
Really?

236
00:13:50,013 --> 00:13:51,557
Some little pipsqueak saw me?

237
00:13:51,640 --> 00:13:53,520
Well, excuse me, so sorry!

238
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:55,100
Shut up.

239
00:13:55,580 --> 00:13:57,357
Now all that remains is for Mr.

240
00:13:57,440 --> 00:13:59,087
Forest Team to do its thing.

241
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:02,297
Fatty and that old hag know
how to get things done.

242
00:14:02,380 --> 00:14:04,637
Catching the king will
be a snap, you'll see!

243
00:14:04,720 --> 00:14:06,480
Oh, joy! I can't wait!

244
00:14:07,860 --> 00:14:09,220
Hear me, rebel army!

245
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:12,600
The Alabasta of old is dead now!

246
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:15,461
This will be our ultimate battle!

247
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:17,720
We go now to capture the capital!

248
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:19,590
Onward!

249
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:21,480
To Alubarna!

250
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:24,380
The king must play!

251
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:26,300
We'll build a new country!

252
00:14:30,420 --> 00:14:31,540
That's absurd!

253
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:35,161
Lord Cobra would never do
anything as mad as that!

254
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:38,420
It must be a mistake! It's
true! And what's more,

255
00:14:38,540 --> 00:14:40,277
the timing between his
disappearance from the

256
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:43,478
palace and his appearance
at Nanohana fits perfectly.

257
00:14:44,780 --> 00:14:46,280
Excuses are useless now.

258
00:14:46,540 --> 00:14:48,817
News of the Nanohana incident
has spread throughout

259
00:14:48,900 --> 00:14:52,076
Alabasta and rebel soldiers
everywhere are responding.

260
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:53,230
Even worse,

261
00:14:53,313 --> 00:14:56,517
citizens who once had faith in the king
are now taking up arms against him.

262
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:58,117
